**Constraints for 14 Mill Wynd:**
- It is in the **Glenarrow Town Centre conservation area**.
- It is not a listed building.
- It has no tree preservation order.

**Council guidance on outbuildings:** Garden rooms and sheds under 2.5 metres high, behind the front wall of the house, and covering less than half the garden usually do not need an application. Conservation areas and listed buildings are treated differently.

**What this means for you:** Because 14 Mill Wynd is in a conservation area, the usual exemptions may not apply in full. I can't give a formal opinion on whether your garden room needs permission. To find out, please check the following:
- The height of the building (under or over 2.5 m)
- Its position (behind the front wall of the house or not)
- The proportion of the garden it would cover (under or over half)

If it fails any of these, or if you're unsure, you should submit a planning application. If you have an existing application reference for this property, send it to me and I can look up its status.
